# =============================================================================
# backend/.env.example — SUPERSEDED
# =============================================================================
#
# The environment file for this project is generated, and it lives at the
# repository root: `.env.example`. It is built from the settings the app reads
# (`backend/app/core/config.py`) plus the keys read outside that model, so it
# cannot drift from the code.
#
#     cp .env.example .env      # from the repository root
#
# The app resolves that file by path (`BASE_DIR / ".env"`), so it is the same
# store whatever directory the process starts in, and it is the one the Keys tab
# writes (`EnvKeyStore`). A `backend/.env` is not read.
#
# This copy exists only because older instructions told you to copy it. It
# listed keys nothing reads — an `OLLAMA_BASE_URL` setting that was retired, and
# four `TITLE_LLM_*` keys from a retired provider universe — so its contents were
# removed rather than corrected: one generated home beats two hand-kept ones.
